WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:06.720
We are back. This review exercise aimed to&nbsp;
identify the library needed to enable writing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:14.080
the streams of text on lines 5 through 7 to&nbsp;
memory without writing that text to a file.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:19.400
Such a task requires the io library,&nbsp;
and that code is on line 1. Secondly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:24.520
we need the method from the IO library that&nbsp;
will, again, allow us to write this text&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:30.960
to memory. The StringIO method is the one&nbsp;
needed, so after the equal sign on line 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:38.160
I’ve added io.StringIO with a set of parentheses.&nbsp;
Remember that most anything in Python is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:49.440
case-sensitive. I will run this code, and we&nbsp;
see all three lines of the stream. By the way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:59.400
do you know the answer to this question? It is&nbsp;
PI R squared, R being the radius of a circle.

